  "worked_solution": "First, we complete the squares for the variable ${x}_{2}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-2({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-2({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-2{({x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+2{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-2{({x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}^{2}-2{({x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, performing the change of variables\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}={x}_{1}, \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the pair of intersecting lines ${x}_{1}=\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2}$ and ${x}_{1}=-\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
